# Phase 18 compatibility gate log — ProcessQueue negative batch size
# Recorded: 2026-10-23 01:02:11 UTC
# Code revision: c3b53fcb

## Oracle finding

Pinned Java constructs `new ArrayList<>(batchSize)` before reading the current
clock or taking the ProcessQueue lock. Negative capacity throws
`IllegalArgumentException: Illegal Capacity: -1` without changing
`lastConsumeTimestamp`. Rust's direct method previously asserted and panicked.
It now returns `ProcessQueueError::InvalidBatchSize` before state mutation, and
the internal positive batch call site handles the new result type.

The invoked Java fixture and Rust facade comparison check both exception text
and a seeded timestamp. Fixture SHA-256:
`63be1fa9e086d577e01c6a5ac1eba6089e30f237f9bf03b178832dc22496772d`.

